<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Operational modules</p>
      <h1>Operational Modules</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        The booking and enquiry workflow is the live intake layer. Records, invoices and reporting show how that structured work can continue behind the website.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="stat-grid">
      <article class="stat">
        <strong><%= bookingStats.total %></strong>
        <span>Sample requests</span>
      </article>
      <article class="stat">
        <strong><%= bookingStats.typeCount %></strong>
        <span>Intake patterns</span>
      </article>
      <article class="stat">
        <strong><%= stats.recordsTotal %></strong>
        <span>Demo records</span>
      </article>
      <article class="stat">
        <strong><%= stats.invoicesOpen %></strong>
        <span>Open invoices</span>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="card-grid module-grid">
      <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Working module</p>
        <h3>Booking & Enquiry Workflow</h3>
        <p>
          Appointment, venue/resource, group/visit and recurring requests feed one shared admin queue with review logic, status handling and CSV export.
        </p>
        <a class="btn" href="/book">Open public intake</a>
        <a class="text-link" href="/admin">Open shared admin</a>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Operational history</p>
        <h3>Records Module</h3>
        <p>
          Public-safe record list and detail views show how accepted work can preserve context after the initial request.
        </p>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/modules/records">Open records module</a>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Financial visibility</p>
        <h3>Invoice Workflow</h3>
        <p>
          Demo invoice states and detail views illustrate how financial administration can sit alongside operational records where it is needed.
        </p>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/modules/invoices">Open invoice workflow</a>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Reporting layer</p>
        <h3>Reports & Export Capability</h3>
        <p>
          Summary metrics and export routes demonstrate how structured data can support admin review, finance and decision-making.
        </p>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/modules/reports">Open reports view</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
